    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0964" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4061/81: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-23T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 23—3:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Reference my No. 77, March 20.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d820-f1"/> As to any
                    action taken by the Film Commission at its meeting to put regulations into
                    effect, no definite information is forthcoming.</p>
                <p>Since the text of these regulations, in incomplete form as mentioned in my
                    telegram 72 of March 16 (namely, without indication of approval by Herriot nor
                    otherwise given binding effect), has appeared in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Matin</hi> and in trade papers, however, our commercial attaché has seen
                    the Director-General of the Fine Arts, who is ex officio chairman of the Film
                    Commission, about the matter.</p>
                <p>In a despatch leaving today,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d820-f2"/> additional details
                    are given in order to facilitate the Department in instructing me further. If
                    any other developments take place before the receipt of this information, and if
                    informal action seems advisable, I shall proceed according to authority granted
                    in Department’s telegram 74, of March 15, noon, and shall cable my report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
